# 🚀 Day 19 - Min Stack

## 📌 Phase

**Custom Data Structures**

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Build a **Min Stack** that stores temperature readings and can instantly return the **minimum recorded temperature**.

The stack should support:

* 📥 `push()` - Add temperature
* 📤 `pop()` - Remove temperature
* 🔍 `get_min()` - Get minimum temperature

## 💡 Example

```text
Input:  [32, 28, 35, 25, 30, 22]

Minimum: 22°C
```

After removing `22`:

```text
Minimum: 25°C
```

## 🧠 Approach

The Min Stack uses **two stacks**:

```text
Main Stack       Min Stack
    ↓                ↓
   32               32
   28               28
   35
   25               25
   30
   22               22
```

The **Min Stack** keeps track of the current minimum value.

This allows us to find the minimum without scanning the entire stack.

## ⚡ Complexity

| Operation   | Complexity |
| ----------- | ---------- |
| `push()`    | O(1)       |
| `pop()`     | O(1)       |
| `get_min()` | O(1)       |

**Space Complexity:** `O(n)`

## 🌍 Real-World Applications

* 🌡️ Temperature monitoring
* 💰 Financial systems
* ☁️ Cloud infrastructure
* 📊 Monitoring systems
* 🚨 Real-time alert systems

## 🏆 Key Learning

Through this challenge, I learned:

* 📚 Custom data structures
* 🥞 Stack implementation
* ⚡ O(1) minimum lookup
* 🔄 Managing multiple stacks
* 📈 Time & space complexity

